  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building SMART Anti-Poaching Methods to Protect Tigers and their Prey in Russia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2010, one of the Wildlife Conservation Societys primary activities in Russia has been to target conservation efforts at key protected areas with Amur tigers. The goal is to improve law enforcement at these sites to increase population sizes of tigers and their prey, and to increase the effective protected area of these source sites. WCS works with protected area staff to utilize a management system called SMART (Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool), which increases the efficiency and accountability of their anti-poaching programs. To date, these efforts are paying dividends. All protected areas where WCS have partnered, have shown improvements in anti-poaching efforts, and tiger numbers have largely remained stable or increased. Project objectives are to: (1) Support proper implementation of the SMART system at seven existing protected areas with tigers in Russia; (2) Improve capacity at sites to provide protection; and, (3) Foster institutionalization of SMART patrol monitoring and management at these sites.</narrative>
  </description>
